{
  "dom_id": "step-e10868",
  "name": "Example: Identifying True Statements Regarding Sums and Products",
  "problem": "Find the product of all three cube roots of unity.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the principal cube root of unity is \n\n$$\nz=e^{2\\pi\\text{i}/3},\n$$\n\nand that any cube root of unity is of the form $z^k$ for $k=0,1,2.$ Also, we have $z^3=1.$\n\nTherefore, the product of all three roots is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{0}\\cdot {z}^{1}\\cdot {z}^{2} & ={z}^{0\\,+\\,1\\,+\\,2} \\\\  & ={z}^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
